      "content": "Gentle parenting is a soft failure that breeds entitled slackers, not strong individuals. When you constantly prioritize a child's feelings over necessary discipline, you are teaching them that their whims are law, eroding their respect for structure. This permissive approach actively stunts the development of grit, replacing necessary boundaries with endless negotiation. Ultimately, you are raising emotionally fragile people who crumble the moment life demands real accountability.",
